  "body": "## Evidence\n\nReplaying all five local short-circuit detectors over **153,198 real production requests** — every stored prompt decompressed and re-tested:\n\n| rule | lifetime fires |\n| --- | ---: |\n| `title_generation_skip` | 3,122 |\n| `suggestion_mode_skip` | 130 |\n| `quota_mock` | **0** |\n| `prefix_detection` | **0** |\n| `filepath_extraction_mock` | **0** |\n\nThe three zeroes are **not a pattern that drifted by a word.** Clustering every billed request under 12,000 characters in that log by its opening system lines gives 1,835 requests, and **not one belongs to any of the three families** — no `<policy_spec>` prefix-detection prompt, no `Command:`/`Output:` filepath-extraction prompt, no `max_tokens=1` quota probe. Claude Code stopped sending these shapes. There is nothing left to fit a pattern to, which is why this is a deletion and not a rewrite.\n\n## Removed\n\n```\nFAST_PREFIX_DETECTION            + fast_prefix_detection\nENABLE_NETWORK_PROBE_MOCK        + enable_network_probe_mock\nENABLE_FILEPATH_EXTRACTION_MOCK  + enable_filepath_extraction_mock\n```\n\nEvery surface: the `Settings` field, the `ConfigFieldSpec` in the admin manifest, the `.env.example` block, the detector, the handler, the `OPTIMIZATION_HANDLERS` / `OPTIMIZATION_RULES` entries, and the tests.\n\n`api/command_utils.py` existed only for two of these rules and had no other importer — deleted, along with its `free_claude_code` shim. `_single_user_turn` in `detection.py` had no surviving caller and went with them.\n\n**1,087 lines removed, 13 added.**\n\n## Deliberately kept\n\n- **`is_safety_classifier_request`** — lives in the same module but is *not* one of the five. `handlers/messages.py` uses it to suppress thinking on safety-classifier requests. Byte-identical, still covered by 6 tests.\n- **`_request_system_text`** — title detection still needs it.\n- **`tests/api/test_request_utils.py` was pruned, not deleted.** It also holds `TestTitleGenerationRequest` and `TestGetTokenCount`, and both `smoke/capabilities.py` and `smoke/features.py` point the `count_tokens_contract` capability at that exact path. Deleting it would have broken a smoke contract silently.\n\n## Version: MINOR, not MAJOR — deliberately\n\nThe repo rule lists \"removed env vars\" under MAJOR, whose stated purpose is *\"migrations users must act on\"*. **There is no migration here, and that was verified rather than assumed:**\n\n```\n$ env -i HOME=/tmp/fresh FAST_PREFIX_DETECTION=true \\\n    ENABLE_NETWORK_PROBE_MOCK=false ENABLE_FILEPATH_EXTRACTION_MOCK=1 \\\n    uv run python -c \"from ... import Settings; Settings()\"\nSettings() constructed OK with all three removed vars set\nhas fast_prefix_detection: False\n```\n\n`Settings.model_config` sets `extra=\"ignore\"`, so a leftover key never raises. The keys toggled rules that have **never once fired**, so removing them cannot change any observable behaviour. Spending a major version on a no-op would make the versioning signal less useful, not more. Called out explicitly in the release notes instead. *(Owner's call, asked and answered.)*\n\n**One real file effect:** `unmanaged_env_values()` preserves a key only if it is in the manifest, in `settings_env_aliases()`, or `FCC_`-prefixed. These are now none of those, so a stale line disappears from a user's `~/.fcc/.env` on their next admin Save. Harmless — it configured nothing — but it is a write to their file and the release notes say so.\n\n## Verification\n\n**6 mutations, each asserted applied, whole file per run, no `-k` filter, all CAUGHT:**\n\n| Mutation | Caught by |\n| --- | --- |\n| Re-add `fast_prefix_detection` to `Settings` | `test_removed_settings_fields_are_gone` |\n| Re-add `ENABLE_NETWORK_PROBE_MOCK` to `.env.example` | `test_removed_env_keys_are_gone_from_env_example` |\n| Re-add the `ENABLE_FILEPATH_EXTRACTION_MOCK` spec | `test_removed_env_keys_are_gone_from_the_admin_manifest` |\n| Re-add `\"quota_mock\"` to `OPTIMIZATION_RULES` | `test_removed_rule_names_are_not_published` |\n| Re-add `is_quota_check_request` | `test_removed_handlers_and_detectors_are_gone` |\n| Restore `api/command_utils.py` | `test_command_utils_module_is_gone` |\n\nA new contract test file pins every surface, so a **partial** revert fails rather than half-landing — which is the failure mode this kind of deletion actually has.\n\n**Full suite** (rebased onto the context-length fix, so both changes coexist): `4,789 passed, 8 failed, 26 skipped`. All 8 are `tests/scripts/test_install_ps1_*`, the standing Windows baseline. `ruff format`, `ruff check`, `ty`, suppression grep: clean.\n\n## Deliberately not done\n\n- `tests/api/test_request_utils_filepaths_and_suggestions.py` keeps its now half-stale name. `smoke/` indexes sibling test paths by string; the rename is cosmetic and not worth the re-verification.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **The admin runtime section loses three advanced toggles.** The section-rendering contract test still passes, but this was not confirmed in a browser. Low risk — the section still has other fields — and the upcoming optimizer page rebuilds this area anyway.\n- If a user genuinely relied on one of these three toggles, they were relying on a switch for a code path that has never executed. No behaviour can change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti\n",
