    "message": "chore(optimizer): remove three local rules that have never fired\n\nReplaying all five local short-circuit detectors over 153,198 real production\nrequests -- every stored prompt decompressed and re-tested -- gave:\n\n    title_generation_skip     3,122 fires\n    suggestion_mode_skip        130 fires\n    quota_mock                    0\n    prefix_detection              0\n    filepath_extraction_mock      0\n\nThe three zeroes are not a pattern that drifted by a word. Clustering every\nbilled request under 12,000 characters in that log by its opening system\nlines gives 1,835 requests, and not one belongs to any of the three families:\nno <policy_spec> prefix-detection prompt, no Command:/Output: filepath\nextraction prompt, no max_tokens=1 quota probe. Claude Code stopped sending\nthese shapes, so there is nothing left to fit a pattern to.\n\nRemoved, with every surface each one had:\n\n    FAST_PREFIX_DETECTION            + fast_prefix_detection\n    ENABLE_NETWORK_PROBE_MOCK        + enable_network_probe_mock\n    ENABLE_FILEPATH_EXTRACTION_MOCK  + enable_filepath_extraction_mock\n\nSurfaces: the Settings field, the ConfigFieldSpec in the admin manifest, the\n.env.example block, the detector, the handler, the OPTIMIZATION_HANDLERS and\nOPTIMIZATION_RULES entries, and the tests. api/command_utils.py existed only\nfor two of these rules and had no other importer, so it and its\nfree_claude_code shim are deleted. _single_user_turn in detection.py had no\nsurviving caller and went with them.\n\nDeliberately kept: is_safety_classifier_request, which lives in the same\nmodule but is not one of the five -- handlers/messages.py uses it to suppress\nthinking on safety-classifier requests. Byte-identical, still tested.\n_request_system_text stays; title detection still needs it.\n\ntests/api/test_request_utils.py was pruned rather than deleted: it also holds\nTestTitleGenerationRequest and TestGetTokenCount, and smoke/capabilities.py\nand smoke/features.py both point the count_tokens_contract capability at that\nexact path. Deleting it would have broken a smoke contract silently.\n\nVersion: MINOR, not MAJOR, and deliberately so. The repo rule lists \"removed\nenv vars\" under MAJOR, whose stated purpose is \"migrations users must act\non\". There is no migration here and that was verified, not assumed:\nSettings.model_config sets extra=\"ignore\", so a leftover key never raises --\nconfirmed empirically by constructing Settings() with all three set under a\nfresh HOME. The keys toggled rules that have never once fired, so removing\nthem cannot change any observable behaviour. Called out in the release notes\ninstead of spending a major version on a no-op.\n\nOne real file effect: unmanaged_env_values() preserves a key only if it is in\nthe manifest, in settings_env_aliases(), or FCC_-prefixed. These are now none\nof those, so a stale line disappears from a user's ~/.fcc/.env on their next\nadmin Save. Harmless -- it configured nothing -- but it is a write to their\nfile and the release notes say so.\n\nVerification\n- 6 mutations, each asserted applied, whole file per run, no -k filter, all\n  CAUGHT: re-adding the Settings field, the .env.example key, the manifest\n  ConfigFieldSpec, the OPTIMIZATION_RULES entry, the detector function, and\n  restoring command_utils.py. A new contract test file pins every surface, so\n  a partial revert fails rather than half-lands.\n- Startup with all three removed vars set: Settings() constructs, no error.\n- Full suite after rebasing onto the context-length fix: 4,789 passed,\n  8 failed, all tests/scripts/test_install_ps1_*, the standing baseline.\n- ruff format, ruff check, ty, suppression grep: clean.\n\nDeliberately not done\n- tests/api/test_request_utils_filepaths_and_suggestions.py keeps its now\n  half-stale name. smoke/ indexes sibling test paths by string; the rename is\n  cosmetic and not worth the re-verification.\n- The admin runtime section loses three advanced toggles. The rendering\n  contract test still passes, but this was not confirmed in a browser.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
